</div><div class=3D"trow" style=3D"display:flex"><div class=3D"thumbcaption=
">STD computer cards</div></div></div></div>
<p>The <b>STD Bus</b> is a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bus_(co=
mputing)" title=3D"Bus (computing)">computer bus</a> that was used primaril=
y for <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Industrial_control_system" t=
itle=3D"Industrial control system">industrial control systems</a>, but has =
also found applications in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computi=
ng" title=3D"Computing">computing</a>. The STD Bus has also been designated=
 as <b>STD-80</b>, referring to its relation to the <a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Zilog_Z80" title=3D"Zilog Z80">Zilog Z80</a> series <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microprocessor" title=3D"Microprocessor=
">microprocessors</a>. The term <i>STD</i> is in reference to "standard", b=
ut several marketing terms were also promulgated, including <i>simple to de=
sign</i>, <i>simple to debug</i>, and <i>swift to deliver</i>.
</p>
<meta property=3D"mw:PageProp/toc">
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"Description">Description</h=
2><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</=
span><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DSTD_Bus&amp;ac=
tion=3Dedit&amp;section=3D1" title=3D"Edit section: Description"><span>edit=
</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p>The STD Bus uses 6.5" by 4.5" <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E=
xpansion_card" title=3D"Expansion card">expansion card</a> with an <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edge_connector" title=3D"Edge connector">=
edge connector</a> with 56 pins. Many different types of cards have been av=
ailable for the STD Bus, from processing cards, <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Random-access_memory" title=3D"Random-access memory">RAM</a> =
cards, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Input/output" title=3D"Inpu=
t/output">I/O</a> cards, and specialized cards for various applications.
</p><p>The use of the STD bus has declined. From the over one hundred manuf=
acturers of components during its peak, vendor numbers have dwindled to und=
er a dozen, but it is still used by hobbyists, manufacturers and in industr=
ial applications.=20
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"Connector_pin_assignments">=
Connector pin assignments</h2><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D=
"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/inde=
x.php?title=3DSTD_Bus&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D2" title=3D"Edit sect=
ion: Connector pin assignments"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-edit=
section-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p>The STD Bus has a card edge connector with 56 contacts. The pin configur=
ation is as follows. Flow is relative using an STD Bus processor card.<sup =
id=3D"cite_ref-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/STD_Bus#cite_note-1"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>1<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
